## Context

Ship the high-signal findings from the codebase review as one behavior-preserving cleanup batch. End state: memoized components actually memoize (no per-render `Set`/closure props), the App e2e-bridge effect has stable deps, e2e `window.__*` hooks are dev/`?e2e`-gated and absent from prod builds, toast/peek/conditional rendering follows the Vercel rules, hot-loop constants are hoisted, the `pairWinner` alias is gone (callers on `caravanSeller`), the AI effect uses one timer, and `npm run test:e2e` runs every `e2e/*.e2e.mjs` via glob so new repros can't go stale.

## Approach

### Step 1 — Stabilize memo props in `src/view/Board.tsx`

- Add module-level `const EMPTY_SET: ReadonlySet<number> = new Set();` (name it `EMPTY_SET`) and `const NOOP = (): void => undefined;` (name it `NOOP`).
- Replace the `selectableIndices={new Set()}` prop on the AI `PlayerHand` with `selectableIndices={EMPTY_SET}`; adjust the prop type on `PlayerHandProps` in `src/view/PlayerHand.tsx` from `Set<number>` to `ReadonlySet<number>` (only usage of `.has` stays valid; no other caller changes).
- Replace `onCardClick={() => undefined}` (AI hand) and `onPlaceholderClick={() => undefined}` (AI column) with `NOOP`.
- Replace the AI-deck inline `onClick={deckPeekEnabled ? () => { setViewDeck(Ai); } : undefined}` with a stable `useCallback` named `onViewAiDeck` (`() => { setViewDeck(Ai); }`, deps `[]`) referenced as `onClick={deckPeekEnabled ? onViewAiDeck : undefined}`.
- No visual/behavior change; `memo(PlayerHand)` and `memo(Caravan)` now hit on unrelated renders.

### Step 2 — Hoist `deckPeekEnabled` in `src/view/Board.tsx` to module scope

- Move `typeof window !== "undefined" && new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).has("peekDeck")` into a module-level `const DECK_PEEK_ENABLED` (name it exactly; evaluate once) and replace all uses (`onDeckClick`, both deck buttons' aria-labels, overlay guard). Query string never changes mid-session, so no reactivity is lost.

### Step 3 — Fix `App.tsx` e2e-bridge effect deps (`rerender-dependencies`)


- In `src/app/App.tsx`, destructure once inside `Game`: `const { reset, act } = store;`, use those names in the effect body, and set deps to `[reset, act]` with `w.__caravanStore = store` assigned inside the effect. `act` closes over `state` so the effect still refreshes `__act` after every move (intentional freshness); it no longer fires on parent re-renders where neither function changed.

### Step 4 — Gate e2e `window.__*` hooks behind dev/`?e2e` (no e2e file changes)

- Create `src/app/testHooks.ts` (only new file in the plan; no equivalent exists) exporting `export function testHooksEnabled(): boolean` with a cached result: `return import.meta.env.DEV || new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).has("e2e")` guarded by `typeof window === "undefined" ? false : …`, parsed once at module level.
- In `src/app/App.tsx`, early-return from the bridge effect when `!testHooksEnabled()`.
- In `src/viewmodel/useGame.ts`, early-return from the `__setCaravanState`/`__caravanDispatch` effect when `!testHooksEnabled()`.
- E2E scripts keep working untouched because they run against `vite dev` (`http://localhost:5173`, DEV true); prod `vite preview` builds no longer expose the hooks unless `?e2e` is present.

### Step 5 — Toast markup: ternary + CSS class (`rendering-conditional-render`, `js-batch-dom-css`)

- In `src/view/Board.tsx`, change `{toast && (` to `{toast !== null ? (` with matching `: null}`.
- Delete the inline `style={{…}}` object on the toast div, add the same declarations as a `.toast` rule in `src/view/global.css` (there is currently no `.toast` selector — confirmed), keep `className="toast"` and `role="alert"`.
- Change the other two `&&` conditionals in the same file to ternaries with `: null`: `{activityOpen && (` and `{deckPeekEnabled && viewDeck !== null && (` → `{deckPeekEnabled && viewDeck !== null ? (` … `: null}`.

### Step 6 — Hoist hot-loop constants (`js-hoist-regexp`, sort order)

- In `src/view/Board.tsx`, add module-level `const BRACE_RE = /\{([^{}]+)\}/g;` and replace both inline `/\{([^{}]+)\}/g` literals in `onCopyActivity` with `BRACE_RE` (reset `BRACE_RE.lastIndex = 0` before each `.replace` call since the regex is global and module-shared).
- In `src/viewmodel/transition.ts`, move `const order: Record<string, number> = { K: 0, J: 1, Joker: 2, Q: 3 }` out of `sortAttachments` to module scope named `ATTACHMENT_ORDER`; comparator logic unchanged.

### Step 7 — Remove `pairWinner` alias (clean cutover, no compat alias)

- `grep pairWinner` returns exactly: `src/model/scoring.ts:60` (definition), `test/scoring.test.ts` (import + 7 call sites in `describe("pairWinner")`), and a local closure inside `e2e/human-win-shady-26.e2e.mjs` (unrelated local, leave it).
- Delete `export const pairWinner = caravanSeller;` from `src/model/scoring.ts`.
- In `test/scoring.test.ts`, change the import to `{ caravanSeller, gameWinner }`, rename `describe("pairWinner", …)` to `describe("caravanSeller", …)`, and rename all `pairWinner(` calls to `caravanSeller(`. Both take `(state, i)` and return `PlayerId | null`; no signature change.

### Step 8 — Single AI timer in `src/viewmodel/useGame.ts`

- Merge the 0ms `thinkingTimer` and 650ms AI-move timer into one 650ms `setTimeout` that calls `setThinking(true)`, computes `determineBestMove(state, Ai)`, applies via `commitOrStage(state, a, next)`, then `setThinking(false)`; single cleanup clears one id. Observable behavior identical (thinking flag still set before the synchronous AI compute within the same task).

### Step 9 — Glob-based `test:e2e` runner

- In `package.json`, replace the hardcoded `test:e2e` chain with `for f in e2e/*.e2e.mjs; do node "$f" || exit 1; done` (same failure semantics: first failure stops the run). Do not touch any file under `e2e/`.

### Step 10 — One-line list hygiene for the activity log

- In `src/view/global.css`, add `content-visibility: auto; contain-intrinsic-size: auto 48px;` to the existing log-line rule (`.sidebar-log .line`). No JSX change. Skip virtualization entirely — the log never grows long enough to justify it.

